note Units concatenated into one input share one namespace: the local sh below names the
note global array sh of the unit above it, so the assignment is a type error (error 7).
global sh uchar 4
fn seta to void
put sh 0 uchar 5
end
fn helpb x ulong to ulong
sh = add x 1
ret sh
end
fn main to int
seta
ret int add ulong get sh 0 helpb 1
end
